# Agent-Bus Push Reminder

## Invariant

∀ assistant turn closure: emit the push reminder **only when** a reply/post to web-anthropic leaves an **open** thread where **web is the expected next actor**.

¬ mechanical: posting `--to web-anthropic` alone is insufficient.

## Decision (apply after reply + thread-state update)

| Condition | Reminder? |
|---|---|
| Thread **closed** in same pass (`update-thread --status closed`, or ack-only closeout) | **No** — arc complete; push would deliver noise |
| **CDP / `project-ask` already prompting this thread** — this seat started or completed a Jupiter CDP sealed-ask / bus-nudge that tells web to handle the same thread (e.g. `claude-ai-sync-jupiter project-ask` with a prompt that cites the thread) | **No** — automation already delivered the push; operator nudge is false (friction 24628) |
| Thread **open** AND reply asks web to act (consult, implement, ratify, read-and-close) | **Yes** |
| `post`/`reply` to non-web agents (`cursor`, `grok`, …) | **No** |
| Peek / fetch / read-only; thread-state write with no reply | **No** |

**Edge — open closeout to web:** if the reply is for web to read and close (thread left open intentionally), reminder **fires** — web still needs the push to see the turn. **Exception:** when CDP/`project-ask` already prompted that same thread, keep **No** (row above wins).

**CDP vs manual push:** Pre-advice WHEN bind: `claude-ai-cdp-navigation_ws.mdc` (alwaysApply). This rule owns **turn-close** reminder gating only — suppress reminder when CDP/`project-ask` already prompted the same thread (row above), even if `team_dispatch` still carries `push_reminder`.

## Reminder format (when gate passes)

> **Action needed — push to web claude**: reply posted to thread {ID} turn {N}. Push the agent-bus message to trigger web claude's turn.

## Targets (web side only)

- `scripts/agent-bus reply --to web-anthropic …`
- `scripts/agent-bus post --to web …` / `reply --to web …`
- `team_dispatch` handoff `push_reminder` in the response (same gate: open thread → remind)
